詹姆斯，祝你那事好运。

288
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:40,400
I've been here before.
我之前也来过这里。

289
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,820
Remember, Patty worked in Epsom town government
记得，帕蒂曾在埃普索姆镇政府工作过

290
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,340
for three decades.
三十年。

291
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:47,020
She's been to the police station before.
她之前也去过警察局。

292
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:48,860
And maybe because of that,
而且可能正是因为这样，

293
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,140
she doesn't sound all that nervous.
她看起来并不太紧张。

294
00:17:51,140 --> 00:17:53,540
She even cracks a joke with the cops.
她甚至和警察开了个玩笑。

295
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,260
Just a few minutes into their chat,
仅仅几分钟的交谈中，

296
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:57,460
Patty mentions she didn't eat lunch
帕蒂提到她没吃午饭

297
00:17:57,460 --> 00:18:00,060
and Lieutenant Keir offers her some almonds.
并让警官基尔给她一些杏仁。

298
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:01,220
A few almonds, yeah.
几颗杏仁，是吧。

299
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:02,060
We have some almonds.
我们有杏仁。

300
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,460
And some water?
还有水吗？

301
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,020
They're not sealed.
它们没密封。

302
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:05,860
No, that's okay.
不，这样可以。

303
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:06,700
Okay.
好的。

304
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:08,660
But, because I don't think you're trying to poison me,
但，因为我觉得你不是想毒害我，

305
00:18:08,660 --> 00:18:09,500
so I'm all set.
所以我已经准备好了。

306
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,340
No, I'm all set.
不，我已经准备好了。

307
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:11,180
But,
但，

308
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:12,540
some water.
一些水。

309
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:14,100
A poison joke,
一个毒药玩笑，

310
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:17,260
with the cops questioning her about her missing husband.
警察在问她关于她失踪丈夫的事。

311
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:21,340
Maybe it seemed like the perfect icebreaker in Patty's head.
也许在帕蒂的脑海中，这看起来像是一个完美的开场白。

312
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:27,340
After some more chit-chat, Detective Elphick of the New Hampshire State Police gets down to it.
聊了会儿天后，新罕布什尔州警察局的侦探埃尔菲克终于开始认真调查。

313
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:30,340
Sure. So when's the last time you saw Jay?
对，那么你最后一次见到杰伊是什么时候？

314
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:36,340
I see him every day up here.
我每天都看到他在那边。

315
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:43,340
Okay, let me think. I have to work backwards here.
好吧，让我想想。我得从后往前推。

316
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:50,340
See him coming.
看到他来了。

317
00:18:50,340 --> 00:19:01,340
This is February.
现在是二月。

318
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:12,340
I thought he was at his brother's all winter, so it was definitely in October.
我一直以为他整个冬天都在他哥哥家，所以肯定是在十月。

319
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:17,340
in October, October 23.
十月，具体是十月二十三日。

320
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:20,060
Okay.
好的。

321
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:26,260
Patty explains that by the previous October in 2023,
帕蒂解释说，在2023年上个月的十月时，

322
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:29,660
Jay was feeling humiliated by his dementia.
杰伊因为自己的痴呆而感到羞辱。

323
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:31,540
He didn't want all the Christmas tree customers
他不想让所有圣诞树顾客都看到他那样。

324
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,220
to see him that way.
看到他那样。

325
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:34,440
He wanted to get away.
他想逃开。

326
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:38,780
So he said he wanted to go down and visit his brothers.
所以他说他想下去看看他的兄弟们。

327
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,580
So I'm like, okay, okay.
所以我就像，好吧，好吧。

328
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:45,580
So do you want me to call them and make arrangements
所以你想要我给他们打电话，安排一下？

329
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:47,440
for transportation?
关于交通安排？

330
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:50,980
He said, no, I'll do that when I'm here.
他说，不，我到的时候再处理。

331
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:54,600
And I said, are you sure?
我问，你确定吗？

332
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:57,780
Cause I can call them and talk to them while you're here.
因为我可以趁你在这里的时候给他们打电话，和他们聊一聊。

333
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:01,240
And he said, no, I'll take care of it.
他说，不，我来处理。

334
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,360
Don't worry about it.
别担心。

335
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,600
So I said, okay.
所以我回答，好吧。

336
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,680
And I wasn't bossy.
我也没多管闲事。

337
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,220
If he had a decision about something,
如果他对某件事有决定，

338
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:13,980
I wasn't the type of person to think that I should be the one in charge.
我并不是那种会认为自己该负责的人。

339
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:14,820
Right.
对。

340
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:15,580
So.
所以。

341
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:20,060
So at what point did he, did he leave or did you come home and he wasn't there
所以，他是什么时候走的？你回家时，他不在家吗？

342
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:20,500
one day?
一天？

343
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:26,660
I came home and, uh, he was not there.
我回家时，他根本不在。

344
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:30,300
And I figured that he went with his brother.
我猜他跟兄弟一起走了。

345
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:32,020
They came and picked him up.
他们来把他接走了。

346
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:37,260
Patty says she figured Jay was just at his brother's house out of state.
帕蒂说，她猜杰伊只是去了州外兄弟家。

347
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:43,480
Only by this point Patty knows the police have figured out Jay is not with his brothers
到这时，帕蒂已经知道警方已经确认杰伊并不在兄弟家。

348
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:48,860
So if he's not with the brothers, which he's not with his brothers. Yeah, where do you think he is?
所以，如果他不在兄弟身边，而事实上他确实不在兄弟身边。对，你觉得他现在在哪儿？

349
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:52,000
Good question. I don't have a clue
好问题。我一点头绪都没有

350
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,600
and actually even though I was like
其实尽管我心想

351
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:58,080
You know the dogs
你知道他那些事

352
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:02,960
And I'm like, I don't want them to find him dead. I went in my life somewhere, but
我心想，我不想让他们发现他死了。我曾去过他生活的地方，但

353
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,600
I
我

354
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:07,100
Don't know
不知道

355
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:11,140
If he was to arrange a car service or whatever, how would he pay for it?
如果他要安排个出租车服务或者别的，他是怎么付钱的？

356
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:15,740
Do you guys have not not to get it do you guys have credit cards or how would how would you know?
你们有没有人不打算去拿它？你们有没有信用卡？你们怎么知道？

357
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:22,840
He gave me his credit card. Oh, I don't know month years ago and said I don't want this okay, and um
他给了我他的信用卡。哦，我记不清是几个月前还是几年前，他说他不想拥有这个，好吧，嗯

358
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:27,220
But he had a stash of cash somewhere. Does he have a phone?
但他某处藏了现金。他有手机吗？

359
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:32,340
This is his phone that's his phone he didn't take it. Yeah
这是他的手机，就是他的手机，他没拿走。对。

360
00:21:32,340 --> 00:21:33,180
Yeah.
对。

361
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:39,260
Patty is saying she came home one day to find her husband
帕蒂说她有一天回家发现丈夫

362
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:42,820
of 40 odd years gone, the one with dementia,
已经40多岁了，患有痴呆症的那个人

363
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,900
who's been wandering, can't drive,
一直在乱走，不会开车，

364
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,060
and who left his phone behind,
而且他把手机落在了后面，

365
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:50,420
and assumes he just left to visit his brother out of state,
还以为他只是去州外探望他兄弟而已，

366
00:21:51,660 --> 00:21:54,060
which is why Patty is not even the one
这就是为什么帕蒂根本不是那个人

367
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:55,940
who called to report Jay missing.
那个打电话报告杰伊失踪的人

368
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:58,860
So you haven't talked to him since October.
所以从十月以来你都没和他联系过。

369
00:21:58,860 --> 00:21:59,700
Right.
对。

370
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:02,980
No, haven't seen him or heard from him in October.
不，十月以来都没见过他，也没听到他的消息。

371
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,740
Have you been concerned about where he is at all?
你有没有担心过他现在在哪儿？

372
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,900
Like, what would have been like?
比如，这会是怎样的情况？

373
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:08,300
Well, not until lately because I thought
嗯，直到最近才开始，因为我以为

374
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:09,540
he was with his brothers.
他一直和兄弟们在一起。

375
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:11,340
But would it be unlike him to not talk to you
但这样不和你说话，对他来说是不是很不像他？

376
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:13,340
for all this time?
这么久都不和你说话？

377
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:16,660
Considering the amount of time that he sleeps
考虑到他睡觉的时间这么长，

378
00:22:16,660 --> 00:22:21,620
and he's not like with the pro, you know, not here and now.
而且他不像那种立刻就出现、马上行动的人，你知道吧。

379
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:31,620
I just figured he was spending those few minutes with his brothers.
我只是觉得他可能花了几分钟时间和兄弟们在一起。

380
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:32,620
Not...
不是……

381
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:38,620
Have you ever called the brothers to check on him at all?
你有没有真的联系过兄弟们去确认一下他的情况？

382
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:43,620
Just when we were trying to, when the police came to look for him.
就在这时，我们正想做点什么，警察却来找他了。

383
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:44,620
Okay.
嗯。

384
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:46,620
But I didn't because I'm...
但我没，因为我……

385
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:52,260
He taught me a long time ago not to be pushy about stuff.
他很久以前就告诉我，别对这些事太咄咄逼人。

386
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:57,660
He's an adult. He makes his decisions. Some decisions we make together.
他是成年人了，他做自己的决定。我们一些决定是共同做出的。

387
00:22:57,780 --> 00:22:58,380
Sure.
当然。

388
00:22:58,380 --> 00:23:04,380
And yeah, I could have called him but most of the time he's sleeping so I quit bothering, you know?
是的，我本可以打电话给他，但大多数时候他都在睡觉，所以我干脆不再打扰了，你知道吗？

389
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:07,060
Have you ever thought...
你有没有想过……

390
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:08,420
What was your plan?
你有什么计划？

391
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:13,500
Did you have a plan as in like it gets to a certain month and he's not here and I haven't
你有没有计划，比如到某个月份他都没出现，而我也没听到、没看到过他？

392
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:17,500
heard or seen from him? Like maybe I should start reporting this?
比如，也许我该开始向有关部门报告这件事？

393
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:21,500
Well, no, because I thought he was with his brothers.
好吧，不，因为我以为他和兄弟们在一起。

394
00:23:21,500 --> 00:23:26,500
Right, but if you haven't seen him or heard from him, when you guys haven't had these big periods of separation since 1980,
对，但如果你这些年来一直没见到他、也没听到他的消息，自从1980年以来，你们一直都没有过长时间的分离，

395
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:31,500
you haven't thought like, okay, if it comes to next October and it's been a whole year that I haven't seen or heard from him,
你们没想过，好吗，如果到了明年十月，已经整整一年没见到或听到他的消息，

396
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:35,500
like maybe I should start figuring out what to do?
比如，也许我该开始想想该怎么做？

397
00:23:35,500 --> 00:23:37,500
Well, you guys are doing that now.
好吧，你们现在就是这样做的。

398
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:41,500
But that's not because you called us. At what point would you have called me and said,
但那不是因为你联系过我们。你什么时候会给我打电话说，

399
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,900
and said, hey, my husband's.
然后说，嘿，我丈夫的。

400
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:43,980
Oh, I see.
哦，我明白了。

401
00:23:43,980 --> 00:23:51,980
Well, that's a good question because a couple of reasons.
嗯，这确实是个好问题，因为有好几个原因。

402
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:56,020
Because he told me not to talk about it, which obviously,
因为他说不要跟我说，这显然,

403
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:58,420
now, legally, I have to.
现在从法律上来说，我必须。

404
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:00,860
And what's the other thing?
还有另一件事吗？

405
00:24:00,860 --> 00:24:03,220
Oh, time flies.
哦，时间过得真快。

406
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:04,300
Like, phew.
就像，哎呀，太紧张了。

407
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:09,340
I don't know exactly what the police officers were
我不知道警方在那一刻到底在想什么。

408
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:11,380
thinking in this moment.
在那一刻他们到底在想什么。

409
00:24:11,380 --> 00:24:13,640
But I'll tell you what I thought.
但我可以告诉你我的想法。

410
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:16,340
What the hell is going on?
到底发生了什么？

411
00:24:16,340 --> 00:24:23,540
["The Story of the Dead"]
[《死者的故事》]

412
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:26,060
Usually, when someone's spouse is missing
通常，当一个人的配偶失踪时

413
00:24:26,060 --> 00:24:28,740
and their story about it doesn't make sense,
而且他们关于这件事的解释说不通时,

414
00:24:28,740 --> 00:24:30,980
I might assume the worst.
我可能会认为最坏的情况。

415
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:34,620
But in this case, the story was so bizarre,
但在这情况下，这个故事太离奇了，

416
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:36,780
I didn't know what to think.
我都不知道该想什么了。

417
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:39,220
What was going on in Patty's mind?
帕蒂脑子里在想什么？

418
00:24:39,220 --> 00:24:42,120
Could she really believe what she's saying?
她真的相信她说的话吗？

419
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:45,760
Did Jay wander off and Patty just didn't report it?
杰伊是不是走失了，而帕蒂根本没上报？

420
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:46,800
Would that be a crime?
那会是犯罪吗？

421
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:50,040
And where is Jay?
杰伊在哪里？

422
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:52,720
Was there any chance he was still alive?
他还有可能还活着吗？

423
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:55,580
Or is his body somewhere up on the Christmas tree farm?
或者他的尸体藏在圣诞树上？

424
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:59,460
I was beginning to fall down a rabbit hole.
我开始陷入一个兔子洞里了。

425
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:03,280
And at the bottom of it were a bunch of people
在底部，是一群人

426
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,280
who'd already been down there for months.
他们早就待在那里几个月了。

427
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:11,500
The whole thing is like just a bizarre mystery.
整个事情就像那个骗子警告过我的一样，寻找答案的过程只会变得越来越离奇。

428
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:18,880
It's like all these questions that the town has, the community has are just like unanswered.
就像这些镇上、社区里提出的问题，根本就没有任何答案。

429
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:25,280
And just like the original tipster warned me, the search for answers would only get stranger.
就像那个最初的骗子警告过我，寻找答案的过程只会变得越来越离奇。

430
00:25:30,280 --> 00:25:32,280
You haven't been in any legal trauma rape have?
你从未经历过任何法律上的创伤或性侵吗？

431
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,280
Me?
我？

432
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:33,780
Me?
我？

433
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:35,780
You never had the deal with the legal system, right?
你从未和法律系统打过交道，对吧？

434
00:25:35,780 --> 00:25:37,780
I was on a jury one time.
我曾参加过一次陪审团。

435
00:25:37,780 --> 00:25:39,280
Good for you.
真为你高兴。

436
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:41,780
Honey, let's take a walk up into the woods.
亲爱的，我们去树林里走走吧。

437
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:47,780
Let's see what we can find and get hit over to him with a shovel and buried.
我们看看能发现什么，然后拿把铲子把他打晕，带到他那儿，埋了。

438
00:25:47,780 --> 00:25:53,780
My initial thought was she killed him because that was what I always thought would happen.
我最初的想法是她杀了他，因为那正是我一直以为会发生的事。

439
00:25:53,780 --> 00:25:57,280
No way, no way.
不可能，不可能。

440
00:25:57,280 --> 00:26:00,780
They have no idea how much we love each other.
他们根本不知道我们彼此有多深的爱。

441
00:26:03,280 --> 00:26:12,040
Let me just ask him if he broke a bone or okay now my spirit guides are telling me he
让我先问他有没有骨折，或者好吧，我的灵性导师正在告诉我他

442
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:14,040
had a concussion.
受了脑震荡。

443
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:19,200
She was after me because she didn't like the toilet paper I had ordered for the office.
她追杀我，是因为她不喜欢我为办公室订购的纸巾。

